{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-1806","published":"2026-04-03T11:10:49Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:19:45.883396422Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-4775"],"summary":"libtiff security update","details":"This  provides support for the Tag Image File Format (TIFF), a widely used format for storing image data. The latest version of the TIFF specification is available on-line in several different formats.And contains command-line programs for manipulating TIFF format image files using the libtiff library.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA flaw was found in the libtiff library. A remote attacker could exploit a signed integer overflow vulnerability in the putcontig8bitYCbCr44tile function by providing a specially crafted TIFF file. This flaw can lead to an out-of-bounds heap write due to incorrect memory pointer calculations, potentially causing a denial of service (application crash) or arbitrary code execution.(CVE-2026-4775)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libtiff","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP3","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/libtiff&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.6.0-7.oe2403sp3"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["libtiff-4.6.0-7.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libtiff-debuginfo-4.6.0-7.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libtiff-debugsource-4.6.0-7.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libtiff-devel-4.6.0-7.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libtiff-static-4.6.0-7.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","libtiff-tools-4.6.0-7.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["libtiff-help-4.6.0-7.oe2403sp3.noarch.rpm"],"src":["libtiff-4.6.0-7.oe2403sp3.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["libtiff-4.6.0-7.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","libtiff-debuginfo-4.6.0-7.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","libtiff-debugsource-4.6.0-7.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","libtiff-devel-4.6.0-7.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","libtiff-static-4.6.0-7.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm","libtiff-tools-4.6.0-7.oe2403sp3.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-1806.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libtiff"